  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-31T06:37:20.976Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've encountered a lot of people, especially beginner creators just getting their first model on quest, or even professionals who wanted to port their model and weren't aware, and its a pretty common issue to run into, even for models that don't need vertex colors, since the VRChat mobile shaders force the vertex colors to be used. It doesn't need to prevent an upload, just advise the player that they are there and that it may cause issues for the android build. I'm sure it would go a long way to make things easier and more immediately obvious as to why their model looks weird. \nI've included a proof of concept i whipped up in a few seconds in Photoshop to show my idea.",
